     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like a possible error, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily is **5,100 mg/day** of metformin. The labeled maximum is **2,550 mg/day** for immediate-release and **2,000 mg/day** for extended-release, so this order is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**Common orders this may have been meant as:**\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, e.g., 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day, a common maintenance dose)\n\nWhich dose did you intend? If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the above-maximum dose. Also, should it be immediate-release or extended-release?"
      }
     ],
